.TH "CASCADE" "1" "Jan 01, 2026" "0.1.0-beta7" "Cascade"
.SH NAME
cascade \- Cascade CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.sp
\fBcascade\fP \fB[GLOBAL OPTIONS]\fP \fB<COMMAND>\fP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.sp
\fBcascade\fP is the CLI to the Cascade Daemon \%<>\&.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-server <IP:PORT>
The Cascade server instance to connect to. This option takes priority
over the \fBCASCADE_DAEMON\fP environment variable. [default: 127.0.0.1:4539]
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-log\-level <LEVEL>
The minimum severity of messages to log [default: warning] [possible values:
trace, debug, info, warning, error, critical].
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print the help text (short summary with \fB\-h\fP, long help with \fB\-\-help\fP).
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print client version.
.UNINDENT
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B CASCADE_DAEMON
The Cascade server instance to connect to.
.UNINDENT
.SH COMMANDS
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
\fBcascade\-health\fP(1)
Check the health of Cascade.
.TP
\fBcascade\-zone\fP(1)
Manage zones.
.TP
\fBcascade\-policy\fP(1)
Manage policies.
.TP
\fBcascade\-keyset\fP(1)
Execute manual key roll or key removal commands.
.TP
\fBcascade\-tsig\fP(1)
Manage TSIG keys.
.TP
\fBcascade\-hsm\fP(1)
Manage HSMs.
.TP
\fBcascade\-debug\fP(1)
Debug / troubleshoot Cascade.
.TP
\fBcascade\-template\fP(1)
Print example config or policy files.
.TP
\fBcascade\-info\fP(1)
Show daemon information.
.UNINDENT
.SH SEE ALSO
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \%<https://\:cascade\:.docs\:.nlnetlabs\:.nl>
Cascade online documentation
.TP
\fBcascaded\fP(1)
Cascade Daemon \%<>
.TP
\fBcascaded\-config.toml\fP(5)
Configuration File Format \%<>
.TP
\fBcascaded\-policy.toml\fP(5)
Policy File Format \%<>
.UNINDENT
